From a70323db2e6c9c596ce2adf293b426ba3d955b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-router <build-router@warslop-dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:56:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: per-attempt thinking, menu item provenance,
 usage-limit signal

0008 writes one thinking shape into the shared request body before the combo runs, so every fallback attempt carries the head model's value; a plugin that wants each attempt on its own model's native value (jev-router's menu, UP-10c) could only send none or drop backups. onRoute may now return thinking_by_model {<target id>: {control, value}} (same allowlist as 0008, only targets in the final list), item (a menu id, ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,16}$) and specialist (boolean, only with an item). With a map, the shared-body write is skipped and the plugin combo's handleSingleModel applies applyPluginRouteThinking(b, pluginAttemptThinking(combo, m)) on each attempt's own body copy; a target the map leaves out gets {control:"none"} (client effort cleared), and the global fallback model is sent with none as well. Without a map, 0008's behaviour is unchanged. buildPluginRouteHeaders adds x-router-item, x-router-specialist (yes|no) and x-router-thinking (the answering attempt's value, "default" when no field was sent); the 0009 in-band x_omniroute object carries item, specialist and thinking too.

Usage limits: OpenCode Go limits each model by dollars per 5 hours, week and month, and a spent allowance answers 429 like a short rate limit, so onRouteResult could not tell them apart (kind is rate_limit for both and no error text reaches a plugin). isUsageLimitError (429/402/403 whose text says usage limit, limit reached, quota, allowance, insufficient balance/credit, or Go's "subscribe to OpenCode Go") marks the trace outcome limit:true, and onRouteResult attempts carry limit:true; the text itself still never leaves the host. Unit tests in plugins-onroute and earlyStreamKeepalive.
